    "\n  fragment TimelineCommunicationCardData on CommunicationType {\n    id\n    subject\n    preview\n    communicationContent: content\n    time\n    type\n    direction\n    from {\n      id\n      name\n    }\n    to {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          name\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    tags {\n      label\n    }\n  }\n": types.TimelineCommunicationCardDataFragmentDoc,
    "\n  fragment TimelineEventCardData on EventType {\n    id\n    title\n    description\n    sourceSystem\n    # The connector's catch-all for what has no column — for a social.like\n    # event that is the liked Page's URL, which the drawer offers as a link.\n    metadata\n    startTime\n    endTime\n    timeSource\n    locationName\n    location {\n      ... on PlaceType {\n        id\n        name\n        properties\n      }\n    }\n    previewUrl\n    mediaUrl\n    mediaContentType\n    mediaWidth\n    mediaHeight\n    mediaSize\n    tags {\n      label\n    }\n    # What the event is about, for events that ARE a watch/listen/read: the\n    # first linked content rows, with their resolved preview and player.\n    contents(first: 3) {\n      edges {\n        node {\n          id\n          title\n          contentUrl: url\n          ...RichMediaData\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n": types.TimelineEventCardDataFragmentDoc,
